    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\n`mini.completion` is trying to trigger the completion even on buffers where it's not available.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/735314/232502633-87a5b029-9024-49b1-80b0-1595d8bf6b45.png)\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Have `mini.completion` enabled.\r\n2. In my case, I tried editing a `yaml` file even then I don't have any related server installed.\r\n\r\nThere are the registered lsp servers.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/735314/232504656-af5b2753-19b2-49df-8c8a-0c7bc336e95d.png)\r\n\r\nAnd this is my current `init.lua`\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/fedemp/dotfiles/blob/5cd40a99ec51eb4450dc6efe36f441d73f72a97e/home/.config/nvim/init.lua\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`mini.completion` should not try to trigger onmicompletion.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/735314/232502633-87a5b029-9024-49b1-80b0-1595d8bf6b45.png)\r\n\r\nAn error is shown every time I enter `insert` mode.",
