            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\n'mini.completion' [does try to check](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/completion.lua#L709) if any of attached servers support completion. It *might* fail for certain LSP servers (especially ones forwarded with 'null-ls'), but it shouldn't.\r\n\r\nWould you mind clarifying which servers exactly are attached when the error occurs? I suspect that it is `prettierd` (judging by [your config](https://github.com/fedemp/dotfiles/blob/5cd40a99ec51eb4450dc6efe36f441d73f72a97e/home/.config/nvim/init.lua#L265)) , but it would be more helpful if you'd do the following steps:\r\n- Open buffer and reproduce the error.\r\n- Execute the following command: `:lua vim.fn.append(0, vim.split(vim.inspect(vim.lsp.buf_get_clients(0)), '\\n'))`. This will query the information about currently active clients and paste it at the top of current buffer.\r\n- Copy **the whole table** (it is probably very big, couple of hundreds of lines) and paste here under spoiler. Like this:\r\n````markdown\r\n<details><summary>My active servers in problematic buffer</summary>\r\n\r\n```\r\n<You table goes here>\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n````",
